"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e4cc66ca8d12732927c1792800a25b1185c1c9eaaa624907b6b2897c31c0271", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ddad50d89a7e654e227778d1edb3fdf3accface31fde4703a869f6724ea2414", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we explain the analogue of the\nsheafification construction in a topology.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a topology on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a presheaf of sets.\nFor every <MATH_0005> we\ndefine\n<MATH_0006>\nas a colimit. Here we think of <MATH_0007> as a partially ordered set,\nordered by inclusion, see Lemma <REF_0001>. The transition\nmaps in the system are defined as follows.\nIf <MATH_0008> are in <MATH_0009>, then <MATH_0010> is\na morphism of presheaves. Hence there is a natural restriction\nmapping\n<MATH_0011>\nThus we see that\n<MATH_0012>\nis a directed system as in Categories,\nDefinition <REF_0002>\nprovided we reverse the ordering\non <MATH_0013> (which is what the superscript <MATH_0014> is supposed to\nindicate). In particular, since <MATH_0015>\nthere is a canonical map\n<MATH_0016>\ncoming from the identification\n<MATH_0017>.\nIn addition, the colimit defining <MATH_0018> is directed\nsince for any pair of covering sieves <MATH_0019> on <MATH_0020> the\nsieve <MATH_0021> is a covering sieve too, see Lemma <REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nLet <MATH_0022> be a morphism in <MATH_0023>.\nLet <MATH_0024>. There is a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0025>\nWe can use the left vertical map to get canonical restriction maps\n<MATH_0026>\nBase change <MATH_0027> induces an order\npreserving map <MATH_0028>. And the restriction maps\ndefine a transformation of functors as in\nCategories, Lemma <GROUPOPEN_0001>categories-lemma-functorial-colimit<GROUPCLOSE_0001>.\nHence we get a natural restriction map\n<MATH_0029>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23fce675d0a0d70ec922c63d9007a35150aa17e854e034caa0b302b19210d842", "unit_id": "tag:00ZG:prose-0001"}
